/-!
# A permutation model of the second Conway group

This file defines a permutation model `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2` of the second Conway group `Co₂`: the
subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 2300)` generated by two explicit permutations `Co2.a` and `Co2.b`,
each of order `23`. In the second Conway group the maximal subgroups of shape `U₆(2):2` have index
`2300`, which is the least degree in which that group acts faithfully; the model is meant as its
action on the cosets of such a subgroup.

The two permutations are given by their tables of images, and the point `i` of `Fin 2300` is the
point `i` of the source of the tables (see *Provenance*). Products follow Mathlib's convention
`(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`.

Neither the order of the model nor its transitivity or simplicity is asserted here. The generators
are not the standard generators of `Co₂`, which have orders `2` and `5`: the module
`TauCeti.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Sporadic.Conway.Two.Presentation` gives two permutations of
those orders that generate the model and satisfy the relators of the presentation of `Co₂` on its
standard generators, and so maps the presented group onto the model.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2`: the permutation model of the second Conway group on `2300` points.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.orderOf_a`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.orderOf_b`: both generators have order
  `23`.

## Provenance

The tables of `Co2.a` and `Co2.b` are those of the permutations `co2a` and `co2b` of the
`FiniteSimpleGroups` project (Apache-2.0), file `FiniteSimpleGroups/Sporadic/Co2/Basic.lean` at
commit `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`. That file stores the two permutations and their
inverses as the natural numbers `co2aFlat`, `co2aInvFlat`, `co2bFlat` and `co2bInvFlat`, the image
of the point `i` being the field `i` of width `12`; the tables below list those fields in order, so
the numbering of the points is unchanged. The source's generator script `scripts/build_co2.py`
describes the points as the `2300` unordered pairs `{w, v - w}` of minimal vectors of the Leech
lattice, in its integral scaling, with `v ⬝ w = 16` for a fixed minimal vector `v`. The
definitions of the two permutations are taken from the source; its proofs of the order and the
simplicity of the generated group are not reproduced here.

## References

* KitaKen1 (Kenta), *FiniteSimpleGroups*, `Co2` construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>.
* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, the page of `Co₂`, for the maximal subgroup `U₆(2):2` of index `2300`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/spor/Co2/>.
-/

